WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.070
- My profile says don't
panic, I don't have any legs.

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:05.864
I can still pitch a tent,
but I don't like camping.

00:00:05.864 --> 00:00:07.550
(soft music)

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:09.550
My name is Spencer West.

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:13.440
I am a gay man, and I am
as single as they come.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.990
I think I would consider myself a romantic

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.230
given the opportunity.

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:19.410
Growing up in a small town
here in the United States

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:22.830
in Wyoming and being gay,
there wasn't any examples.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.850
I don't really have any
pre-conceived notions

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:26.150
or touch stones or anything,

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:27.640
which in the beginning
was a little frustrating,

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.710
'cause I'm like well how does this work

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:29.610
and what does this look like?

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:31.210
But now as I've gotten a bit older,

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.340
I realize oh, I kinda
get to make the rules

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:36.100
and get to decide what
that looks like for myself.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.610
I would say that I fluctuate in dating.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.040
I go in spurts where I'm like I'm into it

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:40.930
and I want to meet someone.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:43.350
And then I'm like ugh, this is exhausting.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.320
I used to on like my dating profiles

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:49.220
on like Grindr and Tinder
not disclose my disability,

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:51.610
but I had photos that's like
clearly I don't have any legs,

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:53.330
but sometimes people don't really notice.

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:54.480
I didn't think it was important,

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:55.680
because I thought oh, it shouldn't matter,

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.490
but then I realized what
would happen is I would start

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.470
to chat with someone and get to know them,

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:00.670
and then we'd get to the stage where like,

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:01.700
okay, well maybe we should meet,

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:03.630
and then it would have to
be like oh, by the way,

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.520
I don't have any legs.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.690
And sometimes it would be like
oh, this person blocked me

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:07.970
and doesn't want to talk anymore.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:09.720
Or sometimes it would be like oh,

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.440
well that changes things a little bit.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.590
A it felt like coming
out for a second time.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:15.030
I've got two things to come out about.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.008
Surprise, I'm gay.

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:16.841
Surprise, I don't have any legs.

00:01:16.841 --> 00:01:17.970
And then I thought, well this is silly.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:20.440
I wish that we lived ina
world where it didn't matter,

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:21.510
but I guess it does.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:23.720
So now I address these
things on the app right away

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:25.420
to sort of like just get it done,

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:27.890
so then we can move on
to more meaningful things

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:29.460
like getting to know each other.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:30.720
People want to know where my legs are

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:31.940
and I'll copy and paste that

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.470
from like notes in my phone,

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:35.430
'cause it's like so obnoxious
to type out every time.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:36.730
Well I was born with a genetic disease

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:38.450
that caused the muscles
in my legs not to work.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:39.860
As a kid they removed just below my pelvis

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.030
so I could get around better.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:43.560
It's a lot to type on like a dating app,

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:44.800
so I would copy and paste it.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:46.300
Then the next question
people always wanted

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.560
to know is do you have a penis

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:49.570
and can you have sex?

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:51.607
So like I address, yes I don't have legs,

00:01:51.607 --> 00:01:55.490
and yes I have a penis, and yes it works.

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:56.680
And I try to make a joke about it,

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:57.730
because I think it's important

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:00.300
to like laugh at ourselves
and get other people

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.410
to laugh at the same time,

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:02.910
hopefully that's kinda cute too, you know?

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:05.930
What's interesting though,
is a lot of these profiles

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:08.440
don't have my height or my weight.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.030
So when you have to list those things,

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:11.460
I always keep them blank,
and then people are like,

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:12.480
well, how tall are you?

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.690
And I'm like, two foot seven inches,

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:16.791
and I weigh 85 pounds.

00:02:16.791 --> 00:02:17.624
(laughing)

00:02:17.624 --> 00:02:20.760
What's been nice about
addressing it like that is now

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.790
when people message me,
it's usually the people

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:25.460
that are interested, not just
in the physicality of things,

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:26.870
but like in me as a person.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:28.810
I think it gets people to
see my personality a bit more

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:31.690
and to see past my disability
and this idea of just

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:34.610
being like a sex object and
into like the person itself.

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:35.850
When people contact you, you can tell

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:37.090
whether they're actually interested in you

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.290
or whether they're fetishizing you,

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:40.070
and it's a thing like in
the disability community,

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:42.090
not just like me without legs.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:43.240
I've talked to a lot of other folks

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.720
with disabilities who have the same thing.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.970
It's the curiosity of like,
how does everything work

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:50.190
and I want to like experience
it just to say that I did.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:52.140
The other that I'll get,
I'll just get a message

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.880
being like, you're such an inspiration.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.080
I'm so proud of you, you're so brave

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:57.320
for being on this app.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:00.020
This is coming from a
genuine, like nice place,

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:00.853
but I don't think people understand

00:03:00.853 --> 00:03:02.430
that it sounds so condescending,

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:04.620
'cause how I interpret it, largely,

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.340
is like oh man, if I was in your position,

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:08.840
I wouldn't date, I wouldn't fall in love.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.620
This would be awful, I'd
probably stay at home

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.950
and cry all day, like
whatever that would look like.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:15.060
I don't know, I usually respond by saying

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:18.010
that's really nice, but why is me wanting

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:19.740
to fall in love inspiring?

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:21.050
Or why is that brave?

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:23.410
I'm not doing anything
that you're not doing.

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:24.640
I just happen to not have legs

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.111
and don't have to spend money on shoes.

00:03:26.111 --> 00:03:29.090
(soft music)

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:31.270
A couple of years ago I met someone.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:33.750
He was from New York, so it
just so happened I was gonna

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.690
be in New York like a few weeks later,

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:37.020
so I messaged him and I was like hey,

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:38.600
I'm gonna be here, let's go out.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:40.890
And he was like amazing, let's do that.

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:44.457
And it was probably
like the best first date

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:46.460
that I have ever had.

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:48.930
I felt like I was living my
best Carrie Bradshaw life,

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:50.280
like in New York City.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.270
He said this restaurant that was nearby.

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:54.620
We were both really nervous,
we each like had a drink

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:56.410
and ordered our food,
and instantly started

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:58.960
to relax, we had this
amazing conversation.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.310
So after dinner, we wanted
the date to continue.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:03.410
It was one of those like the
conversation was so good.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:05.300
So he was like, do you wanna
just like go for a walk?

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.480
And I was like

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:07.313
yes.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.500
We're starting to walk,
and we turn the corner

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.800
and it's all these
beautiful, brown stones,

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.050
and so he was do you wanna just like sit

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:15.280
on the stupe of this brown stone and chat?

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:17.890
And I was like yes, and so in my mind,

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:18.723
I was like playing it cool,

00:04:18.723 --> 00:04:19.877
I was just like yeah, yeah sounds good.

00:04:19.877 --> 00:04:23.160
And so we like sit down on the stairs.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.020
We're like chatting and really connecting

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:26.790
and really having this
lovely conversation.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:28.850
You know, like we start
like getting a little closer

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:30.930
and getting a little closer, and then,

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:31.763
(record scratching)

00:04:31.763 --> 00:04:34.210
I don't know, I feel like I
was reading the signals right,

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:35.420
but I think he panicked and he was like,

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:36.380
can I give you a hug?

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:38.430
And I was like, wah wah, but sure!

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:40.200
And like okay, we'll start there.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:43.190
So we hugged, we kept
talking, and as we're talking,

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:44.550
I'm like sort of looking at the sky

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.000
and looking at him, it's starting

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.420
to get grayer and grayer, and pretty soon,

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:50.500
it like lightly starts to rain,

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:52.680
and he's like we should
probably go inside.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:53.690
And I was like wait, wait, wait,

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:55.330
I feel like we have to take advantage

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:58.707
of this opportunity, and I just
leaned in and I kissed him.

00:04:58.707 --> 00:05:00.560
We made out in the rain for a little bit,

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:03.900
which was like so romantic and so hot,

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:07.200
and then we walked to like a nearby bar

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.610
and just like had a couple drinks

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:12.200
and just like sat in the
corner and just chatted

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:15.250
and cuddled, and then he walked me home

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:18.060
to my friend's apartment, and that was it.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:20.610
For me, it was like love exists.

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:23.630
People are romantic, and even for someone

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:25.350
with a disability, it didn't matter.

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:27.050
This is what love is supposed to be like,

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:28.480
and this is what genuine connection is

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:31.250
and this is what every
first date should be like.

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:34.560
I hope people just have a
deeper understanding of A,

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:37.700
what it's like to be queer
and to have a disability,

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:39.950
and for folks to recognize that yes,

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:42.450
we are sexual people, like everyone else,

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:44.440
but I think it's important for us

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:47.850
to get to know one another
and to have that visibility of

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:49.660
that just because I have a disability,

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:52.140
doesn't mean I want to date,
and doesn't mean I don't want

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:54.560
to have sex, I have all
of those same feelings

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:57.010
and urges as everyone else does,

00:05:57.010 --> 00:05:59.320
and I think it's important
that we all recognize that

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:02.290
and encapsulate that
to see the whole person

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:05.002
and not just these segments of them.

00:06:05.002 --> 00:06:07.502
(soft music)

